---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import AffiliateLink from "../../components/AffiliateLink.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Zelda: Breath of the Wild — Still Worth Buying in 2026?"
  description="A buying guide for The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild: why it still holds up, editions, and where to buy cheapest."
>
  <article class="post">
    <h1>Zelda: Breath of the Wild — Still Worth Buying in 2026?</h1>
    <p class="meta">Nintendo Switch · Updated 2026-08-05</p>

    <p>
      <strong>The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild</strong> reinvented the open-world
      formula and remains one of the best-selling Switch games ever. Even with Tears of
      the Kingdom out, BotW is the better starting point for most new players.
    </p>

    <h2>Why it still matters</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Massive open world</strong> — climb, glide, and explore with almost no hand-holding</li>
      <li><strong>Cheaper than ever</strong> — years past launch, it sits in Nintendo's budget "Selects" range</li>
      <li><strong>Great first Zelda</strong> — if you've never played one, this is the friendliest entry</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Editions and DLC</h2>
    <p>
      The base game is enough for most. The <em>Expansion Pass</em> adds a harder mode
      and a sizable post-game chapter; buy it only if you finish the main story and want
      more. Watch for the bundled "Special Edition" only if the extras appeal to you.
    </p>

    <h2>Where to buy cheapest</h2>
    <ul class="buy-list">
      <li>
        <AffiliateLink
          network="amazon"
          href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Zelda+Breath+of+the+Wild+Switch"
          cta="Check on Amazon"
        />
      </li>
    </ul>

    <p class="note">
      Prices change frequently — always verify on the store before purchasing.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .post { padding: 1.5rem 0; max-width: 720px; }
  .post h1 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
